    id: "trainer-catalog-alpha-collective",
    locationId: "location-alpha-collective-alpha-collective",
    content:
      "# Alpha Collective\r\n\r\n## Locations\r\n\r\nSector 01\r\nThe busiest of all of the Alpha Collective's hollow asteroids, Sector 01 is famed as a docking yard and trading post for anyone seeking a good deal. Trade permits and tariffs are extremely low in this area which causes a large array of traders to show up no matter what their wares. To the outside observer, this state-sized asteroid also houses a rather large proportion of humans.\r\nThe truth is that these 'humans' are actually a large population of Tuffles, gathering connections and powerful allies while waiting to strike at their old enemies.\r\nDock 006\r\nDock 006 is famous as the ironically safest port in the Alpha Collective, considering it is used almost purely by pirates. This alcove is where pirates come to sell their wares or buy things with ill-gotten currency, and anyone who upsets that trust with clients and merchants tarnishes the entire piracy business. May the Kais have mercy on the upstart who thinks he's above this code, because the pirates will not.\r\nSector 02\r\nWhen people think of the Alpha Collective, they're largely thinking of Sector 02. This sector has the highest crime rate out of any 'civilized' area in the Southern Galaxy. The reason for this is that the thieves and murderers who want to make a name for themselves or 'make it big' come here seeking prey, not realizing that half of the denizens are doing exactly the same thing.\r\nTo counter this, thousands of bodyguards offer their services in the area and it has become a frequent profession, though many are scam artists as well. If one needs an assassin or mercenary hired, this is the place to find the best. The only problem is surviving long enough to find them...\r\nBig Cycle's\r\nDescendant of a nearly dead Changeling clan, Cycle is a mercenary captain that has amassed the most power on Sector 02. If you absolutely need something done, and you have the money for it, you want Cycle's men.\r\nSector 03\r\nThe most guarded of all sectors, Sector 03 is the generator sector that supports the entirety of the Alpha Collective. This station is filled with well contained nuclear reactors and has mile long rows of complex technology used to process the gravity and atmospheric needs and shifts in the other sectors. Nobody has ever gotten in without Lord Frost's permission; at least, nobody willing to risk talking about it.\r\nSector 04\r\nSector 04 is both a vacation resort and a horrific place to be trapped. This hollowed asteroid is filled with an ocean containing all sea life found on the destroyed planets of the Frieza empire. Unfortunately, this means hundreds of immense predator species. The protected areas are amazing places to house a spa or cruise, but the six hundred miles of unprotected ocean are filled with squatters, small islands, monstrous sealife, and pirates.\r\nSector 05\r\nThis Sector is the prison for the rest of the Collective. An entire city-state of a prison, this hollowed asteroid is not as well linked to the others; escapees risk space exposure if they leave their cell for too long. The Changeling guards have no problem with this, but then again, neither do the Changeling prisoners.\r\nThe cells have KI-nullifying technology and the prisoners are treated harshly when the guards deem to deal with them, though many are simply ignored because there are so many cells to handle.\r\nThe Undersector\r\nRumors abound of an entire sector hidden underneath Sector 05, one that is run by an entirely different organization. The Changelings scoff at such an idea, but no official investigation has been done.\r\nSector 06 - 08\r\nThe similar looking sectors of 06-08 are all residential sectors for the Changeling race, each approximately the size of a small country with fine agriculture, gravity, and a dome roof that emulates a sun. While the Alpha Collective is largely considered a place for shady dealings and cutthroat mercantile, these three sectors were preserved for the Changeling race to exist without being bothered (too much) by visitors.\r\nThe cities within hold large white and red towers with banners hanging from the rooftops to the 2nd level to show which of the Changeling clans controls the building. The crime rate of these sectors is extremely low; any infraction at all leads to the Death Penalty for those without the proper connections. Generally, the closer you get to the Changeling Palace the more power the clans hold.\r\nSector 09\r\nThis sector is thought by many to be closed, but the truth is that the Tuffles have over a dozen cities hidden within the state-sized asteroid. It is here that the Tuffles used their cloning pods 200 years ago to replenish their population and prepare to strike back against the Saiyans. Oddly enough, no strike has been made.\r\nThe Tuffle population here often travels via gene-encoded teleport pads to Sector 01 and back, keeping a facade of a mild human population on the Alpha Collective while they make trade with those passing through.\r\nLocations source: https://www.tapatalk.com/groups/dragonballlegacy1/alpha-collective-locations-t59.html\r\n## Martial Arts Trainers\r\n\r\nMove names are grouped by the same categories used in the trainer thread. Full move descriptions and mechanics are omitted.\r\nFreestyle — Duke\r\nSkills: Any non-Afterlife\r\nAdvanced Attacks: Any non-Afterlife\r\nBlocks: Any non-Afterlife\r\nKurokonwaku — Frozt & Breez\r\nMasteries: After-Image Mastery; Control Mastery\r\nSkills: Shadow Stalker; Killer Gaze\r\nAdvanced Attacks: Poison Mist; Vampiric Lust; Sweet Dreams; Firebreath; Kick Them When They're Down; Bloodletter; Cannonball; Empty Beam; Shockwave; Dismissive Kick; Dark Energy Spiral\r\nSignature Techniques: Black Hole Slam; Fade To Black\r\nBlocks: Aerial Maneuvers; Smokescreen\nAkaikaru — Aysse\r\nMasteries: Rage Mastery; Blazing Speed Mastery\r\nSkills: Vehemence\r\nAdvanced Attacks: Blown Fuse; Torpedo Kick; Spinebreaker; Rolling Thunder; Chained Strikes; Anger Management; Letting Off Steam; Stampede Rush; Accelerated Shoulder Tackle; Sniping Shot\r\nSignature Techniques: Chained Mauler; Burn Out\r\nBlocks: Backflip; Gone In A Sixtieth of A Second\r\nAoyosumu — Suno\r\nMasteries: Leverage Mastery\r\nSkills: Opportunist; Reversal of Fortune\r\nAdvanced Attacks: Bullwhip; Weeping Willow; Breakout; Trapped Strikes; Frost Wind Technique; Slow Charge; Super Arm Bar Takedown; Elevated Kick\r\nSignature Techniques: Creeping Death; Epitaph To War\r\nBlocks: Screening; Stepping On Toes\r\nHaokiru — Mod Zero\r\nMasteries: Immortal Mastery; Karmic Chameleon Mastery\r\nSkills: Mind Reading; Advanced Behavior; High Threshold; Willing Sacrifice\r\nAdvanced Attacks: Halcyon Blow; Phantom Barrage; Tornado Uppercut; Lion's Roar; Phoenix Tackle; Rising Dragon Wave; Vengeance Wave\r\nSignature Techniques: Soul Breaker\r\nBlocks: Display of Endurance\r\nKiihakai — Yobi\r\nMasteries: Fierce Focus Mastery\r\nSkills: Eagle Eye; Ki Shield; Overload\r\nAdvanced Attacks: Aerial Beam; Downward Spiral; Static Shot; Aura Clash; Brutal Knockback; Fade Attack; Triple Shot\r\nSignature Techniques: The Heartstopper; The Rising Sun\r\nBlocks: Negative Outburst\r\nMidorikatai — Mizore\r\nMasteries: Critical Mass Mastery; Bonecrusher Mastery\r\nSkills: Energy Gorged\r\nAdvanced Attacks: Ankle Buster; Breaker Breaker; Omega Strike; Flapjack; One-Two Punch; Palm Crusher; Power Drill; Fallaway Slam; Jawbreaker\r\nSignature Techniques: Monster Mash; Violence Party\r\nBlocks: Cross Stance\r\nTrainer source: https://www.tapatalk.com/groups/dragonballlegacy1/alpha-collective-martial-arts-trainers-t60.html\r\n",
