      "# Brutus\r\n\r\n## Locations\r\n\r\nFallback used: The dedicated Locations thread was inaccessible because Tapatalk returned repeated rate-limit errors. The planet-level forum description is included below until the dedicated thread can be retrieved.\r\nPlanet overview (fallback)\r\nBrutus' landscape is very similar to Earth, blue water, green fields, etc. However, unlike Earth, it is made up of two large islands connected by a man-made bridge. Brutus is technologically backwards, though consisting of some beautiful structures that are reminiscent of Earth's Roman and Greek Empires, including gigantic coliseums that are the prime source of entertainment.\r\nLacking any means of transportation other than one's own feet, the Brutii are naturally physically impressive specimens since they are expected to do hard manual labor from birth and walk long distances all the time.\r\nLocations source: https://www.tapatalk.com/groups/dragonballlegacy1/brutus-locations-t422.html\r\n## Martial Arts Trainers\r\n\r\nMove names are grouped by the same categories used in the trainer thread. Full move descriptions and mechanics are omitted.\r\nFreestyle — Duke\r\nSkills: Any non-Afterlife\r\nAdvanced Attacks: Any non-Afterlife\r\nBlocks: Any non-Afterlife\r\nMidorikatai — Gigantus\r\nMasteries: Any\r\nSkills: Any\r\nAdvanced Attacks: Any\r\nSignature Techniques: Any\r\nBlocks: Any\r\nTrainer source: https://www.tapatalk.com/groups/dragonballlegacy1/brutus-martial-arts-trainers-t423.html\r\n",
